Enhancement: Add `--migrate` option to `backup` for zip archives

Until now, backing up the contents of a zip archive required extracting
it to disk first.

`backup --migrate <file.zip>` now backs up the entries of a zip archive
in place, preserving the paths inside the archive. The archive is never
extracted to disk: entry contents are decompressed on the fly and
streamed to the repository, so memory usage stays bounded no matter how
large the archive is. `restore` reproduces the entries byte for byte,
including permissions and modification times. The archive is validated
before the repository is opened, and the backup always behaves like
`--force`, as a zip archive has no meaningful parent snapshot.

